menu "DBG_PROBE"
	config DBG_PROBE
		bool "Enable dbg_probe (register-level debug probe)"
		default n
		help
			Two-layer register-level debug probe. Frontend dbg_probe_* APIs
			encode a compact self-describing frame and hand it to a backend
			sink. Default backend: UART direct write (per-core; core0->UART1,
			core1->UART2), force-on power/clock, bypassing the UART driver
			framework. When disabled every API compiles to a static-inline
			no-op.

	config DBG_PROBE_TIMESTAMP
		bool "Attach AON-RTC timestamps to _ts probe frames"
		depends on DBG_PROBE
		default y
		help
			When set, the dbg_probe_*_ts() variants read the AON RTC counter
			and emit an 8-byte frame: a full 32-bit tick for value16 kinds, or
			a 16-bit short tick (bytes 2..3) for the 32-bit payload kinds
			(TASK/U32). If the AON RTC is not yet enabled the frame degrades to
			the no-ts form (a probe never blocks on an idle RTC). When unset the
			_ts variants behave like their plain counterparts.

	config DBG_PROBE_RAMRING
		bool "Tee probe frames into a per-core RAM ring buffer"
		depends on DBG_PROBE
		default y
		help
			Always-on RAM sink: every runtime frame is also copied into a
			per-core circular buffer (overwrite policy). With no UART attached,
			a memory dump (or the `dbgp dump` CLI) recovers the most recent probe
			timeline; the self-describing frames let the parser resync after the
			wrap point. Per-core rings keep the hot path spinlock-free. A small
			separate "critical" ring isolates exception frames from the default
			high-volume stream. When unset the RAM sink compiles to no-ops.

	config DBG_PROBE_SYNC
		bool "Inject a periodic sync frame (corruption recovery + drop detect)"
		depends on DBG_PROBE
		default y
		help
			Every DBG_PROBE_SYNC_EVERY user frames (per core), emit a sync frame
			(U32 kind + SYNC module) carrying a 32-bit running frame counter and a
			short timestamp. The host parser uses it to re-anchor after a corrupted
			byte run and to detect how many frames were lost in a window. When
			unset, no sync frames are emitted (the counter logic compiles out).
endmenu
